  "verbalization": "Acetylsalicylic Acid, a well-known nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drug (NSAID), is linked to Cyp2c9 through its inclusion in the Nonsteroidal Anti-inflammatory Compounds class. This class includes oxaprozin, meloxicam, and mefenamic acid, all of which bind to Cyp2c9. The shared classification and binding relationship suggest a general mechanism by which NSAIDs interact with Cyp2c9, likely through their common structural features or pharmacological properties. The lowest common ancestors of these compounds—Cyclooxygenase Inhibitor and Organic Aromatic Compound—highlight potential molecular pathways that may underlie the interaction. While the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated, the evidence points to a consistent interaction between NSAIDs and Cyp2c9, possibly through shared metabolic pathways or enzyme inhibition. The integration of these pathways underscores the role of Cyp2c9 in drug metabolism, particularly in the context of NSAID action.",
